# Finish the job, then ask to publish

Work only on `main`. At the start of any work in this repo, check out `main` and pull `origin/main` before the first edit. Stay on `main`. Do not create a feature branch.

Complete the full job on `main` (implement, test, commit locally). Railway (`https://books.spodazo.com`) deploys from `main` only. A commit that has not been pushed is not live.

Then ask the user to publish. Their shortcut is `pp`.

When they say `pp`: commit if needed and `git push origin main`. No pull request. No merge step. Do not ask for extra confirmation.

Never force-push `main`. Never update git config. Never skip hooks.
